  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CCLPHH-Digital Transformation in justice</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Acknowledging difficulties faced by informal workers, especially the female ones, including limited knowledge and access to job opportunities, health care services, education, not to mention limited capabilities to follow and complete complicated administrative procedures required, CCLPHH proposed tech-integrated solutions to enhance the quality and effectiveness of communication models, legal aid and consultancy to provide informal workers in Nghe An with better access to state rights. All are implemented on virtual platforms with the support of digital applications and social sites for the increased accessibility of the focus group. Indeed, the project&#x2019;s targeted groups are informal workers, women, girls, people living with HIV and people at high risk of HIV infections. At the end of the project, the expected outcomes include 2500 people with instant access to legal communication activities throughout the project implementation; 400 to 500 people are provided with legal consultancy and aid to protect their legitimate rights and benefits in accordance with state laws. The initiative is piloted in 5 communes of Que Phong district, Nghe An province, namely, Kim Son, Muong Noc, Chau Kim, Tien Phong and Quang Phong. CCLPHH will harness its close partnershipwith Lawyers Association of Nghe An province to implement legal aid and consultancy activities. Simultaneously, communications activities are projected to be more effective as of its collaboration and support from People&#x2019;s Committee of Que Phong district.</narrative>
  </description>
  <participating-org role="4" type="11">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&apos;CCLPHH works in health and HIV/AIDS, in particular:
1. Providing legal aid for people who are affected by HIV/AIDS, as well as poor people and beneficiaries of social welfare.
2. Communicating for laws and policies in relation to health and HIV/AIDS.
3. Participating in building and contributing to draft laws on health and HIV/AIDS.
4. Conducting scientific research in law and policy regarding Health, HIV/AIDS.
5. Implementing projects in the field of health and HIV/AIDS.
6. Carrying out other activities in accordance with Vietnam#s law</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Center for Consulting on Legal and</narrative>
